            ],
            'faqs' => [
                ['Can I work as a psychologist after this?', '<p>No, and Gatehouse says so itself in the specification: the qualification provides academic preparation for postgraduate study in psychology and does not confer eligibility to practise as a psychologist or deliver psychological interventions. Becoming a registered or chartered psychologist is governed by the regulator in whichever country you intend to work, and it typically involves accredited degree study plus supervised practice. This is a step on that longer road, not a shortcut around it.</p>', 1],
                ['I studied something unrelated. Is that a problem?', '<p>It is the reason the qualification exists. Gatehouse calls it a broad bridging award for learners from psychology and non-psychology backgrounds who need a comprehensive academic foundation across the core areas before MSc-level study. The entry criteria even list education, health, social care and business as relevant experience, so a background in any of those is treated as useful rather than as a gap.</p>', 2],
                ['Is this the same as the Qualifi Level 7 Diploma in Psychology?', '<p>No. They share a name and a level, which causes genuine confusion. The Gatehouse qualification is 610/7550/4 with 360 guided learning hours and units coded from T/652/1920. The Qualifi one is 610/2064/3 with 480 guided learning hours and an entirely different unit set. Different awarding bodies, different content, separate certificates. Check the QAN on any offer letter so you know which you are signing up to.</p>', 3],
                ['What does the assessment involve?', '<p>Coursework and a Portfolio of Evidence, with no written examination. Across the six units you build written work and supporting evidence, which the centre signs off unit by unit before internal moderation. Gatehouse then moderates externally. The research methods unit asks you to produce an ethically informed research proposal at postgraduate standard, so expect a substantial written piece towards the end.</p>', 4],
                ['Will a university accept it for MSc entry?', '<p>Gatehouse designed it with MSc progression in mind, but admission is always the receiving university\'s decision, not the awarding body\'s. Before enrolling, approach the specific universities you are interested in and ask whether they will accept a 120-credit Ofqual-regulated Level 7 diploma as preparation for their course, and whether they require an accredited conversion course instead. Get the answer in writing.</p>', 5],
                ['Who teaches it and what will it cost?', '<p>Gatehouse awards the qualification but does not teach. Delivery runs through an approved centre under an exclusivity agreement, so availability is limited rather than open to any provider. The £206 figure Gatehouse publishes is the registration fee a centre pays for the qualification, excluding VAT. Your tuition is a separate price set by the centre, and it varies internationally, so ask for the full cost in writing.</p>', 6],
            ],
            'meta_title' => 'Level 7 Diploma in Psychology | Gatehouse Awards, UK',
            'meta_description' => 'Ofqual-regulated Level 7 Diploma in Psychology from Gatehouse Awards. A 120-credit bridging award for MSc preparation. Not a licence to practise. QAN 610/7550/4.',
        ],
