            'hero' => 'The tightest qualification in Qualifi\'s Level 3 range: three subjects covering transaction records, cost and management information, and the maintenance of financial records. Sixty credits, aimed at building the foundation for accountancy work or for further study.',
            'overview' => [
                'This is a deliberately narrow award and better for it. Where Qualifi\'s other Level 3 business qualifications survey marketing, people, operations and culture, this one stays on the books. Its stated aim is to give learners the foundation required for a career in financial management and accountancy across a range of organisations, or to move on to further study in the subject.',
                'Three subjects do the work. Financial Transactions Record-keeping establishes why entries have to be accurate and what happens when they are not. Cost and Management Information introduces the internal numbers a business uses to make decisions, which is a different discipline from reporting to the outside world. Financial Records Maintenance covers keeping the records in order once they exist.',
