                'Care work rewards people who can think as well as cope, and it tends to promote them without preparing them. Supervising a team, arguing a case about quality, reading a policy properly and understanding why a service user\'s circumstances are what they are — these are different skills from direct care, and this award treats them as such.',
                'Eleven subjects carry it. Academic study skills and reflective practice come first, because the step up to this level is partly an academic one. Communication, healthcare policy, sociology of health and ill health, and the principles underpinning the sector build the understanding. Managing people, quality management, partnership working, working with service users with complex needs and a research project complete it.',
