            'faqs' => [
                ['Why are only eight subjects listed for 240 credits?', '<p>We noticed that too, and we cannot explain it from what Qualifi publishes. Comparable Qualifi awards at 240 credits typically list twelve subjects. The likeliest reading is that the page shows one half of a combined Level 4 and Level 5 programme, but the page nowhere says so, and we are not going to assert something the awarding body has not stated. Ask your centre for the full Centre Specification before you enrol.</p>', 1],
                ['What does "dove-tail into a top-up year" mean in practice?', '<p>It means the Level 5 content is built to line up with the final year of a UK undergraduate degree, so a university can slot you in at that point rather than making you start over. It describes the design intent. Whether a particular university accepts you, and onto which course, is that university\'s decision — On sister awards at this level, Qualifi prints that condition beside the route itself.</p>', 2],
                ['I manage a hotel but have no qualifications. Can I apply?', '<p>On the published entry routes, yes. Managerial work experience combined with ambition and clear career goals is listed as a way in by itself, with no certificate alongside. The centre assesses whether your experience is enough, so describe the scale of what you run — team size, budget, responsibilities — rather than just naming your job title.</p>', 3],
                ['Where does this sit against the Level 3 hospitality diploma?', '<p>Almost entirely. The Level 3 award is open entry, 120 credits, and introduces the two industries at a basic level. This expects a Level 3 or 4 qualification, managerial experience or a first degree, runs to 240 credits, and deals with destinations, sustainability, culture and your own research. One is where you start; this is where you prepare to run things.</p>', 4],
                ['Is there an English requirement?', '<p>Not one that Qualifi publishes for this particular award. Its page lists three entry routes and none mentions IELTS or a minimum age, although other Qualifi diplomas at the same level do state 18 and over with IELTS 6. Rather than assume another award\'s rules apply, ask your centre. Centres may also set their own language checks regardless of what the awarding body requires.</p>', 5],
                ['What is the research project?', '<p>It appears as one of the eight published subjects, and Qualifi gives no further detail about its length, format or assessment on the qualification page. Based on where it sits, expect an independent piece of work applying what you have studied to a real problem, supervised by your centre. The centre will tell you the scope and the deadlines, since it designs and assesses the delivery.</p>', 6],
            ],
