            'is_active' => false,
            'hero' => 'Twelve fixed subjects, nothing to choose, and a clear arc from logical and physical networking up to routing, switching and whole-estate design. Qualifi states the position without hedging: all twelve are mandatory to receive 240 credits.',
            'overview' => [
                'Networks have a habit of being understood in pieces. Someone knows how to crimp a cable, someone else configures switches, a third person drew the topology years ago and has left. Studying the subject properly means seeing it as one thing, from the physical layer up to a design that somebody can hand over.',
                'That arc is visible in the published subject list. Logical IT networking and physical IT networking establish how networks are reasoned about and how they are actually built. System administration covers keeping the machines on them running. Network routing and switching deals with moving traffic between them. Network design and administration asks you to plan the whole thing.',
