            'sort_order' => 236,
            'is_active' => false,
            'hero' => 'Qualifi calls this a semi-technical award about cyber security as a workplace management discipline. Threat and risk, forensics and cryptography sit beside business continuity, incident communications and strategic leadership. Built for whoever has to answer when something goes wrong.',
            'overview' => [
                'When an organisation is attacked, two kinds of people are needed. One group works the keyboards. The other decides what to tell customers, whether to pay, when to involve lawyers, how to keep the business running and who answers to the board on Monday. The second group is who this award is written for.',
                'Qualifi describes it as semi-technical, examining technical cyber security measures alongside the management, project management and leadership skills needed to organise internal and external responses to major incidents. It promises business continuity and disaster management content set inside the digital threat environment, and says the programme is designed and delivered by a mix of academics from business schools and security management teaching roles.',
                'Eleven subjects deliver it. The technical core runs from threat and risk through network and database security to cryptography, incident response and two separate treatments of forensic investigation. Around that sit the managerial subjects: security strategy as laws and policy, sector threats in banking and finance, cyber wars, incident communications, and strategic leadership. Altogether 240 credits, catalogued as 610/3296/7.',
            ],
