            'faqs' => [
                ['Is this a technical course or a management course?', '<p>Both, and Qualifi uses the word semi-technical for exactly that reason. You will meet cryptography, database security, network security and forensics, which are technical subjects. You will also meet strategic leadership, incident communications and security strategy covering laws and policies. The design assumes you need enough technical grounding to follow what your specialists tell you, plus the management capability to act on it.</p>', 1],
                ['Qualifi says the course is flexible and online. Is it?', '<p>That is how Qualifi describes the programme\'s design, and it adds that the format blends easily. Worth remembering, though, that Qualifi awards and regulates the qualification while an approved centre actually delivers it. Whether your centre runs it online, in person or as a mixture is the centre\'s decision, as are intake dates and pace. Confirm the format with the centre before you assume it.</p>', 2],
                ['Does it prepare me for CISSP, CompTIA or similar?', '<p>Qualifi publishes no alignment with any industry or vendor certification, so we will not suggest one exists. These are different kinds of credential: this is a regulated academic qualification assessed by a centre, while industry certifications are vendor or body examinations with their own syllabuses. Many people hold both. If a specific certification matters to your role, treat it as a separate piece of work.</p>', 3],
                ['What is the Level 4 before Level 5 rule?', '<p>Qualifi states in its entry requirements that Level 4 units must be completed before Level 5 units. This extended award combines both halves, and the rule prevents you from attempting advanced material before the groundwork is done. It is published on no other Qualifi award we have examined, and it is genuinely useful — it tells you the shape of your study before you begin.</p>', 4],
                ['Which partner institution offers the degree top-up?', '<p>Qualifi does not say. The progression route is published as "pending a successful application to our Partner institution", and no institution is named anywhere on its website. We are not prepared to guess at one. If a degree is your goal, research universities offering top-up degrees in cyber security or risk management yourself and ask them directly what they make of this qualification.</p>', 5],
                ['How does it differ from the networking and cyber security diploma?', '<p>Clearly, once you compare the subjects. Seven appear on both. What differs is the final four. Here they are managerial: conflict between states, sector-specific threats in finance, how an incident gets communicated, and leadership strategy. On the networking variant those four give way to equipment work — cabling and hardware, server administration, traffic routing, and designing an estate end to end. Pick this one if accountability for the response will land on you; pick the other if you would rather be the person fixing it.</p>', 6],
            ],
