            'hero' => 'A deliberate merge of two Qualifi routes. Seven security subjects meet four networking subjects, with no general IT padding and no leadership content. Qualifi publishes exactly which existing qualifications the units came from, which is rare candour.',
            'overview' => [
                'Securing a network and building one are usually taught apart, which is odd, because the people who do either job well tend to understand both. You cannot defend infrastructure you do not understand, and you cannot design infrastructure sensibly without knowing how it gets attacked. This award puts the two together on purpose.',
                'Qualifi is unusually open about how it was assembled. The page names the four existing qualifications its units were drawn from — the Level 4 and Level 5 diplomas in cyber security, and the Level 4 and Level 5 diplomas in IT networking — each with its own number. The result is a combination rather than a new invention, and knowing that tells you precisely what you are signing up for.',
                'Eleven subjects make it up. On the defensive side: threat and risk, network security with data communications, database security and programming, incident response with forensic investigation, cryptography, digital forensics, and security strategy as laws and policy. On the infrastructure side: physical networking, system administration, routing and switching, and network design. Together they come to 240 credits, catalogued as 610/3042/9.',
            ],
            'highlights' => [
                ['Awarded by', 'Qualifi Ltd'],
                ['Regulated by', 'Ofqual, on the RQF'],
                ['Credits', '240 at Level 5'],
                ['Subjects published', '11'],
                ['Balance', 'Seven subjects on security, four on infrastructure'],
                ['Minimum age', '18'],
            ],
            'snapshot' => [
                ['Official title', 'Qualifi Level 5 Extended Diploma in Networking and Cyber Security'],
                ['Qualification number', '610/3042/9 on the Regulated Qualifications Framework'],
                ['Size', '240 credits at Level 5'],
                ['Subjects published', 'Cyber Security Threat and Risk · Network Security and Data Communications · Database Security and Computer Programming · Incident Response, Investigations and Forensics · Security Strategy: Laws, Policies and Implementation · Physical IT Networking · Cryptography · Digital Investigations and Forensics · System Administration · Network Routing and Switching · Network Design and Administration'],
                ['How it was built', 'Qualifi states that the units were taken from four of its existing qualifications: the Level 4 and Level 5 diplomas in cyber security, and the Level 4 and Level 5 diplomas in IT networking. It publishes each of their qualification numbers, which almost no awarding body does'],
                ['Entry', '18 or over, with no prior qualification published and no experience clause. IELTS 6 or equivalent where English is not your first language, plus normally two references, one preferably academic'],
                ['On the subject list', 'Eleven subjects against 240 credits, with no mandatory or optional split published and no credit breakdown. Your centre can confirm the structure from the Centre Specification'],
                ['Onward routes published by Qualifi', 'A Qualifi Level 7 Diploma · university, to complete a degree · employment in an associated profession. The published progression skips Level 6'],
                ['Certifications', 'Despite the routing, switching and network design content, Qualifi publishes no alignment with Cisco, CompTIA, CREST, NCSC or any vendor programme. None should be assumed'],
            ],
            'benefits' => [
                ['Two disciplines in one award', '<p>Security and networking are studied together rather than one being a footnote to the other.</p>', 'git-merge'],
                ['Published provenance', '<p>Qualifi names the four source qualifications with their numbers, so you can see exactly what has been combined.</p>', 'file-search'],
                ['Real networking depth', '<p>Physical networking, routing and switching, and network design and administration go well beyond an introductory treatment.</p>', 'router'],
                ['Forensics from two angles', '<p>Incident response with forensics, and digital investigations and forensics, both feature as distinct subjects.</p>', 'bug'],
                ['No general IT filler', '<p>Unlike the IT family awards, there is no maths, graphics or PC maintenance content taking up space.</p>', 'terminal'],
