            'is_active' => false,
            'hero' => 'Twelve subjects on hazard control, proactive and reactive monitoring, emergency response and audit, taught alongside the communication, culture and people skills that decide whether any of it is followed. Suitable for part-time study while working.',
            'overview' => [
                'Safety systems fail for two reasons. Sometimes nobody worked out the hazard. More often somebody did, wrote it down, and nothing changed on the ground because the message never landed, the culture rewarded shortcuts, or no one checked. This award is built around both halves of that problem.',
                'Qualifi puts the technical side as hazard and risk assessment and control, monitoring and emergency response systems, and health and safety review and audit. It then names the other side explicitly: effective communication, promoting a positive culture, process management and people management, all taught in an occupational health and safety context rather than in general.',
                'Twelve subjects carry it, including an uncommon pairing — proactive monitoring systems and reactive monitoring systems as separate subjects, which is the difference between catching problems early and learning from them afterwards. Qualifi states the award suits part-time learners in the workplace as readily as full-time learners on placement. It is 240 credits, number 610/6564/X, and its specification was updated in October 2025.',
            ],
