            'faqs' => [
                ['Is this about workplace safety?', '<p>No, and the distinction matters before you enrol. This diploma deals with enterprise risk — strategic exposure, governance, financing, modelling, environmental and corporate responsibility factors. Workplace hazards, accident prevention and safety management systems are a different discipline, and Qualifi covers them in its separate occupational health and safety qualifications. If what you need is a safety role, look at those instead.</p>', 1],
                ['Do I really not need a degree?', '<p>Not according to this page, no. Qualifi states only that applicants must be at least nineteen, alongside the usual language and reference requirements, and publishes no prior qualification requirement at all. That is genuinely unusual at Level 7, where most of its awards ask for a Level 6 qualification or a first degree. Because the silence is striking, we would suggest confirming it with your approved centre rather than assuming — centres may apply their own admission standards on top of what the awarding body publishes.</p>', 2],
                ['What are VaR, CVaR and EVaR?', '<p>They are measures of how much an organisation could lose and how likely that loss is. Value at risk estimates the loss not expected to be exceeded over a set period at a chosen confidence level. Conditional value at risk looks at what happens beyond that threshold, in the tail. Entropic value at risk is a more conservative variant again. Qualifi names all three in its summary without expanding them; the plain-language explanation here is ours, and the depth of treatment is set out in the centre specification.</p>', 3],
                ['One of the published outcomes mentions agreements. Does the course cover contract law?', '<p>Nothing on the page suggests it does. Qualifi\'s first listed outcome refers to understanding the principles and formation of agreements, which is standard contract law phrasing, but no subject in the list touches contract formation and the summary never mentions it. It looks like an outcome that has strayed in from a legal qualification. We have left it out of the learning list above rather than advertise legal content we cannot evidence. If contract law matters to you, ask the centre directly and get the answer in writing.</p>', 4],
                ['Where does it lead afterwards?', '<p>Qualifi publishes three options and we have not added to them: its own Level 8 Diploma in Strategic Management, a university for a top-up towards a master\'s, or employment in an associated profession. The middle one needs care. No partner university is named anywhere, no arrangement is described and no conditions are given. This diploma is not a master\'s degree and does not award one; any university decides for itself whether to admit you and how much of this study counts. Speak to them before you commit.</p>', 5],
                ['What about the timetable and the cost?', '<p>Both sit with the centre, not the awarding body. Qualifi writes, accredits and certificates this qualification without running any teaching, so the length of the programme and its price are decided wherever you enrol. No total qualification time is published here either, so there is no official hours estimate against which to sanity-check a proposed schedule. Ask for intake dates, an expected completion date and an itemised fee, all in writing.</p>', 6],
            ],
